      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n\nEnable graph-safe fused multi-step MTP metadata updates for the FlashInfer sparse MLA backend.\n\n## Claims\n\n\n- Enables draft-decode metadata updates for FlashInfer sparse MLA when DCP is disabled.\n- Refreshes `req_id_per_token` in place using the existing GPU metadata kernel.\n- Preserves CUDA graph compatibility without adding allocations or host synchronization.\n- Keeps the optimization disabled under DCP until its additional metadata requirements are supported.\n\n## Validation\n\n\n\n```bash\npytest -q \\\n  tests/v1/attention/test_indexer_deepseek_v4_slot_mapping.py \\\n  -k flashinfer_sparse_draft_metadata\n```\n\n## Details\n\n\n\nThe FlashInfer sparse MLA metadata builder did not advertise support for draft-decode metadata updates. As a result, fused multi-step MTP decode could not refresh its token-to-request mapping through the graph-safe metadata update path.\nThis change implements update_draft_decode_metadata by rebuilding req_id_per_token from the GPU-resident query_start_loc with compute_token_to_req_indices. The operation writes into the preallocated metadata buffer, matching the existing sparse FlashAttention MLA implementation.\nFused draft metadata refresh is enabled only when `dcp_world_size == 1`, matching the existing FlashAttention sparse MLA behavior. DCP continues to use the existing per-step metadata build path because its indexer refresh also requires rank-local sequence-length and slot-mapping updates (There is a separate [PR ](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54790)already open to enable this for DCP)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
